<title>POLAND: Polish min T-bill prices mostly flat at tender.</title>
<headline>Polish min T-bill prices mostly flat at tender.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The minimum price of Polish 13-week T-bills rose at today's primary auction while the 26-week and 52-week paper was flat on total demand of 2.07 billion zlotys against a 1.4 billion zloty offer, the finance ministry said.  </p>
<p>  T-bill	    8-week  13-week  26-week  39-week  52-week</p>
<p>   new min price    --	94.91    90.20     --	82.14</p>
<p>   (pvs auction)    --     (94.87)  (90.20)    --     (82.14)</p>
<p>   new max price    --	95.03    94.95     --	82.50</p>
<p>   (pvs auction)    --     (95.00)  (90.50)    --     (82.40)</p>
<p>   offer		--	400.0    300.0     --	700.0</p>
<p>   bids recorded    --	989.3    220.1     --	860.4</p>
<p>   bids accepted    --	400.0    209.2     --	700.0</p>
<p>   next auction     --	400.0    300.0     --	600.0</p>
<p>NOTE. Offer and all bids in million zlotys.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
